title: The Primary
subtitle: Clinton or Sanders?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 2016 and month = 1
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.dnc_neutral == 1 && Q.prog_strength >= 28) { Q.primary_leaning = 'sanders'; } else { Q.primary_leaning = 'clinton'; }
!}

= The Primary

The Iowa caucuses are weeks away. The front-runner has the endorsements, the money, and the delegates. The challenger has the crowds, the small donors, and an electrified left.

- @clinton: Consolidate around Clinton.
- @open: Let the voters decide, and mean it.
- @sanders: Back the insurgent.

@clinton
subtitle: A safe path, if she can energize the base.
on-arrival: nominee = "Clinton"; nominee_mod += 0; estab_strength += 3; prog_dissent += 3; unity += 2

The apparatus delivers. The nomination is hers by spring, and the left is not happy.

@open
subtitle: Higher risk, higher energy.
on-arrival: nominee = "Clinton"; nominee_mod += 0.2; enthusiasm += 4; unity -= 2; prog_dissent -= 3; prog_strength += 3

The race is long and the nominee is bruised, but the party is energized and the left feels respected. She still wins, narrowly.

@sanders
subtitle: A radical bet.
on-arrival: nominee = "Sanders"; nominee_mod -= 0.1; enthusiasm += 6; prog_strength += 8; mod_dissent += 8; estab_dissent += 5; unity -= 4; far_left += 3

The party takes the biggest swing in its modern history. The base is on fire. The establishment is terrified. The general election is the test.
